## The width decision (measured, not inherited)
The R6/R8 label pack stores one code per wire in a fixed-width field; the code of
node `n` is `cbase + n` with `cbase = v + 2 = 1773`. R8 packed 16-bit fields and its
densified node count (62478, max code 64251) fit. The d2 word has 64042 nodes, so its
max code is 65815 > 65535: **16-bit fields are insufficient here**, and this module
lays the pack out at 17-bit fields. `width16_fails` / `width17_suffices` below are
the machine-checked halves of that decision.

## What is packed
`SG_slots0`: the initial label state over the slot band only —
`code(wS q) = cbase + hold[q][0]` for `q < NR`, zero elsewhere. `hold` is the frozen,
replay-verified slot->node time line, so this table is certified data, not a guess.
The entry band (`wX`/`wY`, the `v` source-leaf slots) and the temp bands are NOT
part of this seed; they ride the same `hold`/`start` streams once the Rec encoder
lands.

## Deliberately NOT delivered
The `Rec` (= `LInstr`) list: `(code, moves, gates)` per step. Constructing it needs
the R6 `Loc`/GenData encoder (`injS`/`retS` + the `cND` densify pass), absent from
